    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Explain why $n!$ is even for $n\\in\\{2,3,4,5,\\ldots\\}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For $n\\geq2$, $n!$ contains a factor of $2$, so it is even.",
      "worked": "For $n\\geq2$, the product $n!=n(n-1)\\cdots2\\times1$ contains a factor of $2$. Therefore $n!$ is divisible by $2$ and is even.",
